---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const MCP_URL = 'https://cohenholmes-blog-mcp.kaine-cohen.workers.dev/mcp';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Connect your agent to the CohenHolmes MCP — CohenHolmes"
  description="A small, read-only MCP server exposing this blog to any AI agent — how MCP works, exactly what it can and can't do, and how to connect Claude, ChatGPT or your own agent to it."
  canonicalPath="/mcp"
  wide
>
  <meta slot="head" http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'">

  <p class="eyebrow">For AI agents &middot; read-only</p>
  <h1>Connect your agent to the CohenHolmes MCP</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    This blog has a small <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MCP</a> server
    sitting in front of it, so your own AI agent can read it directly instead of
    you copy-pasting links into a chat. Here's how MCP works, exactly what this one is
    allowed to do, and how to point your agent at it.
  </p>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>How MCP works, in short</h2>
    <p>
      MCP (Model Context Protocol) is just a standard way for an AI agent to discover and
      call a small set of named <em>tools</em> a server offers, instead of every integration
      being its own bespoke plumbing. Your agent asks the server what it can do, the server
      lists its tools, and the agent calls one when it's useful to what you asked.
    </p>
    <ol class="flow">
      <li>
        <span class="step-label">Your agent</span>
        <p>Claude, ChatGPT, or anything else that speaks MCP.</p>
      </li>
      <li aria-hidden="true" class="arrow">&rarr;</li>
      <li>
        <span class="step-label">MCP</span>
        <p>A standard request/response format for "what tools do you have" and "run this one".</p>
      </li>
      <li aria-hidden="true" class="arrow">&rarr;</li>
      <li>
        <span class="step-label">This server</span>
        <p>A small Cloudflare Worker exposing exactly three tools. Nothing else.</p>
      </li>
      <li aria-hidden="true" class="arrow">&rarr;</li>
      <li>
        <span class="step-label">The live site</span>
        <p>Every call reads cohenholmes.co.uk itself, at request time. Nothing is cached or stored by the server.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>What it can actually do</h2>
    <p>
      Read-only, on purpose. There is no tool that creates, edits or deletes anything —
      this server can't publish a post, change a word of one, or touch anything else on
      the site. No authentication is needed to use it, because there's nothing behind it
      worth protecting: every tool just reads what's already public.
    </p>
    <div class="tools">
      <div class="tool">
        <code>list_posts</code>
        <p>Every published post, newest first &mdash; title, slug, date, summary, tags.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tool">
        <code>get_latest_post</code>
        <p>Just the most recent post's metadata.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tool">
        <code>get_post</code>
        <p>The full text of one post, by slug.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="fine-print">
      No account, no API key, no stored data of yours anywhere, no secrets on the server.
      The source is public too &mdash; <a href="https://github.com/Kaine-source/cohenholmes/tree/main/mcp-server" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read exactly what it does</a> rather
      than take my word for it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Connect it</h2>

    <div class="connect-card">
      <h3>Claude (Desktop, Claude.ai, Cowork)</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>Settings &rarr; Connectors &rarr; <strong>Add custom connector</strong></li>
        <li>Paste the URL below</li>
        <li>No authentication needed &mdash; leave that as is, and save</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="fine-print">On a Team or Enterprise workspace, only an owner or admin can add a
      connector at the organisation level &mdash; everyone else just finds it already there once
      that's done.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="connect-card">
      <h3>Claude Code (CLI)</h3>
      <p>One command, from any directory (<code>--scope user</code> makes it available in every
      project, not just the one you happen to be standing in):</p>
      <pre><code>claude mcp add --transport http --scope user cohenholmes {MCP_URL}</code></pre>
      <p>Then run <code>/mcp</code> inside Claude Code to confirm it connected.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="connect-card">
      <h3>ChatGPT</h3>
      <p>Needs a paid ChatGPT plan with Developer Mode enabled &mdash; OpenAI's own <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/custom-mcp-server" target="_blank" rel="noopener">connector docs</a>
      list exactly which plans currently qualify and the precise menu path, since both shift from
      time to time. As of writing:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Settings &rarr; Apps &amp; Connectors &rarr; Advanced &rarr; enable <strong>Developer Mode</strong></li>
        <li>Apps &amp; Connectors &rarr; <strong>Create</strong></li>
        <li>Paste the URL below, authentication: <strong>None</strong></li>
        <li>Start a <em>new</em> chat &mdash; existing ones won't pick it up</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="url-box">
      <span class="url-label">Server URL</span>
      <code>{MCP_URL}</code>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Questions worth trying</h2>
    <ul class="questions">
      <li>"What's the latest post on the CohenHolmes blog?"</li>
      <li>"List everything Kaine's written about AI governance."</li>
      <li>"Summarise the ALM post for me in three bullet points."</li>
      <li>"Has he written anything about Conditional Access? What's the gist?"</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="story">
      If your agent can call tools at all, any of these should trigger a real
      <code>list_posts</code> or <code>get_post</code> call &mdash; not a guess from training
      data. That's the actual point of connecting it.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  :root{
    --card:#FCFAF6;
    --line:#E3DFD3;
    --muted:#4A4A5A;
  }
  .eyebrow{
    margin:0 0 16px;
    font-family:var(--font-mono);
    font-size:0.76rem;
    letter-spacing:0.12em;
    text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--accent-text);
  }
  .lede{
    max-width:70ch;
    margin-top:18px;
    font-size:clamp(1.02rem, 1.6vw, 1.18rem);
    color:var(--muted);
  }

  .block{ margin-top:56px; }
  .block > p{ max-width:72ch; }

  .flow{
    list-style:none;
    display:flex;
    flex-wrap:wrap;
    align-items:stretch;
    gap:14px;
    margin-top:24px;
  }
  .flow > li:not(.arrow){
    flex:1 1 200px;
    background:var(--card);
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius:14px;
    padding:18px;
  }
  .flow .step-label{
    display:block;
    font-family:var(--font-mono);
    font-size:0.72rem;
    letter-spacing:0.08em;
    text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--accent-text);
    margin-bottom:8px;
  }
  .flow p{ margin:0; font-size:0.92rem; color:var(--muted); }
  .flow .arrow{
    display:flex;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    color:var(--accent);
    font-size:1.4rem;
    flex:0 0 auto;
    padding:0 2px;
  }
  @media (max-width:760px){
    .flow{ flex-direction:column; }
    .flow .arrow{ transform:rotate(90deg); padding:4px 0; }
  }

  .tools{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap:14px;
    margin-top:22px;
  }
  .tool{
    background:var(--card);
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius:14px;
    padding:18px;
  }
  .tool code{
    font-family:var(--font-mono);
    font-size:0.88rem;
    color:var(--navy);
    background:#EDE8DD;
    padding:0.15em 0.45em;
    border-radius:5px;
  }
  .tool p{ margin:10px 0 0; font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--muted); }
  .fine-print{ margin-top:18px; font-size:0.88rem; color:var(--muted); }

  .connect-card{
    background:var(--card);
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius:14px;
    padding:20px 22px;
    margin-top:18px;
    max-width:72ch;
  }
  .connect-card h3{
    font-family:var(--font-display);
    font-size:1.2rem;
    font-weight:600;
    color:var(--navy);
    margin-bottom:10px;
  }
  .connect-card ol{ margin:0; padding-left:22px; }
  .connect-card li{ margin-bottom:4px; font-size:0.95rem; }
  .connect-card p{ margin:0 0 8px; font-size:0.95rem; }
  .connect-card code{
    font-family:var(--font-mono);
    font-size:0.85rem;
    background:#EDE8DD;
    padding:0.15em 0.4em;
    border-radius:5px;
  }
  .connect-card pre{
    background:var(--navy-deep);
    color:#E8E6F0;
    border-radius:10px;
    padding:14px 16px;
    overflow-x:auto;
    white-space:pre-wrap;
    word-break:break-word;
    margin:10px 0;
  }
  .connect-card pre code{ background:none; padding:0; font-size:0.85em; }

  .url-box{
    margin-top:22px;
    display:flex;
    flex-wrap:wrap;
    align-items:center;
    gap:12px;
    background:var(--navy-deep);
    border-radius:12px;
    padding:16px 18px;
    max-width:72ch;
  }
  .url-label{
    font-family:var(--font-mono);
    font-size:0.72rem;
    letter-spacing:0.08em;
    text-transform:uppercase;
    color:#AFC0FF;
  }
  .url-box code{
    font-family:var(--font-mono);
    font-size:0.88rem;
    color:#E8E6F0;
    word-break:break-all;
  }

  .questions{
    list-style:none;
    margin-top:20px;
    display:grid;
    gap:10px;
    max-width:72ch;
  }
  .questions li{
    background:var(--card);
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius:10px;
    padding:12px 16px;
    font-size:0.95rem;
    color:var(--navy);
    font-style:italic;
  }
  .story{ margin-top:18px; max-width:72ch; font-size:0.95rem; color:var(--muted); }
  .story code{
    font-family:var(--font-mono);
    font-size:0.85em;
    background:#EDE8DD;
    padding:0.1em 0.35em;
    border-radius:4px;
    font-style:normal;
  }
</style>
